\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Thailand floats baht, raises interest rates. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Rajan Moses \par \uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 2 (Reuter) - Thailand sent shock waves through Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday by floating the battered baht, a move which analysts said was a de facto devaluation. \par \par \uc2  In a bid to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from spinning into a freefall the Bank of Thailand also raised its key commercial bank lending rate by two percentage points to 12.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "In order to end uncertainty over Thailand's exchange rate policy, Thailand's exchange rate system will from 2 July 1997 be a managed float," finance minister Thanong Bidaya said. \par \par \uc2  "The value of the baht will be determined by market forces to reflect fundamental economic forces. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Thailand believe the managed float system will benefit Thailand's overall economic development," he said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  In offshore markets, the baht sank to 27.00/28.00 to the dollar from 24.25 on news of the float, which analysts said would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It means they can stand away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they want to," said Chiang Yao Chye, economist at CIBC Wood Gundy in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimate that the Bank of Thailand used up to five billion dollars of its foreign reserves in May to defend the baht after it came under heavy speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  This cut the country's foreign reserves to a two-year low of $33.3 billion at the end of May from around $37.3 billion a month earlier \par \par \uc2  Pressure was expected to mount again soon amid sustained bearish sentiment over the country's economy and moves to rescue its beleaguered financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  "Under the new system movements in the exchange rate are expected to be quite large at the initial stage. However, relative stability should be attained after a brief adjustment period," Bidaya said. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time to achieve policy objectives and guard against excessive baht fluctuations." \par \par \uc2  The statement gave no details on the exact way in which the managed float would work, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said later a baht-dollar reference would be set daily, based on the baht's trading average the day before. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it had "an appropriate rate" in mind in which it expected the baht to move, but gave no details. \par \par \uc2  "However, if the baht goes beyond the approriate rate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chaiyawat Wibulsawasdi told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they would not be surprised if the baht tested 30.00 to the dollar. Thai overnight interbank rates were unqoted on Wednesday because banks were unwilling to lend until the market settled down. In the Philippines, the peso was hit by ripples from the Thai announcement, and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates to counter speculative attacks. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah and Malaysian ringitt were also jolted by the news. \par \par \uc2  Bidaya said domestic confidence in Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate system had remained shaky despite the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had successfully defended the baht in May. \par \par \uc2  "This is a de facto devaluation, but we need to know about the onshore/offshore trading system before we know if the speculators have won," a European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader based in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Thailand has a two-tier exchange rate system which limits offshore trading of the baht. \par \par \uc2  Before the float, it was fixed on a daily basis against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said higher lending rates would not help Thailand's economy, which is burdened with a swollen current account deficit and financial market woes. \par \par \uc2  "The economy's already slowing down, interest rates should be coming down not going up," a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7202zo1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
