\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Lower Early Amid Dlr-Buying By Corps \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1997\par 04:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is lower in domestic spot trading early Monday as Thai corporations rush to convert foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt into baht-denominated debt, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is mixed in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell baht at specified times in the future. One-, two- and three-month premiums rose, although six-month and one-year premiums declined. \par \par \uc2  Around 0228 GMT (10:28 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at 25.89 baht, up from 25.87 baht at the close of trading Friday. The dollar is at 24.70 baht in offshore spot trading, down from 25.55 baht Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders have shown little reaction to the government's shutdown Friday of 16 troubled finance companies. But because devaluation fears remain strong, they said Thai corporations continue to buy dollars to hedge their debt. \par \par \uc2  'A lot of customers are converting dollar loans into baht loans,' a dealer at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar-buying has prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 11th day in a row. In domestic trading the dollar is well outside the upper limit of the band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows it to move against the baht. That indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling dollars at below-market rates to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The band is 25.77 baht to 25.81 baht Monday. The mid-rate is 25.79 baht compared with 25.75 baht Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0253GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6u04r9z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
