\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Data/Amplifier -2: May Data Could Be Bleaker \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1997\par 16:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Thailand pegs its baht to a dollar-denominated basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and doesn't allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuate by more than 0.16% each day. When the dollar moves outside that range, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is obligated to buy or sell U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at below-market rates to rein it in. \par \par \uc2  To maintain the system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to keep interest rates high even when the economy stalls. Prominent Thai government officials, such as Commerce Minister Narongchai Akrasanee, say the system stifled the Thai economy after 1995. Most economists agree that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg is unsustainable in the long run. \par \par \uc2  As Thailand's economy cooled to its slowest rate in a decade last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators began to bet the peg wasn't sustainable in the short term either. As a result, the baht has been attacked at least three times in the last 10 months, and the attacks have become progressively more severe. \par \par \uc2  In the most recent attack, in May, the Bank of Thailand got unprecedented aid from Southeast Asian central banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defense, and other regional central banks, including the Bank of Japan, made supportive statements. But the Thai central bnak ultimately had to resort to informal capital controls to quell the attack, effectively shutting down the overseas forward market for baht. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's data for April portend worse news for May, analysts said. Given the ferocity of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attack this month, the balance of payments deficit for May could exceed 26.6 billion baht, said Dominique Maire, an economist with UBS Securities (East Asia) Ltd. in Bangkok. He said foreign reserves will decline further, signaling growing weakness in Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  defenses. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1403GMT \par \par \uc2  1145 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5t03wzv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
