\par\par \b \uc2  Thai stocks edge down by lunch awaiting bank data. \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 29 (Reuter) - Thai stocks fell by the lunch break on Thursday in a slow session as many investors remained sidelined ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  economic data due later and the resumption of Finance One shares on Friday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The SET Index lost 0.95 points in the morning going into the the break at 561.89. The SET 50 was unchanged at 40.69. Turnover was a meagre 983 million baht. \par \par \uc2  Most economic numbers have already been announced but investors are eager to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves as attacks on the baht earlier this year prompted Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Most economic factors have been absorbed following their release earlier this week ... but investors want to see the international reserves to see how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent in defending the baht earlier this year," said Somchai Trairattanapirom, vice president at Sitca. \par \par \uc2  Maintenance of reserves at around the $38 billion level will be positive for the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  There were nerves in the market surrounding Friday's resumption of trading in stocks of troubled finance firm Finance One Plc after a three month suspension and the collapse of a planned merger, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  With the shares expected to begin trading at well below their 10 baht par value, compared to a last trading price of 23.75 in February, traders said the stock may move the market lower. \par \par \uc2  Speculators gambling on the afternoon's data moved in for banking stocks prior to the break and helped pare most earlier losses, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Krung Thai Bank Plc added 0.25 baht to 28.50, Siam City Bank Plc added 0.75 to 15.50. Finance and securities firm Dhana Siam Plc topped the active list and lost one to 19.25. \par \par \uc2  --James Mclean (662) 652 0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5t04s4x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
