\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand, China sign securities repo agreement. \b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 27 (Reuter) - The central banks of China and Thailand banks have signed a bilateral repurchase agreement as part of regional cooperation among Asian countries to stabilise their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during emergencies. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said the pact allows one \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to borrow U.S. dollars from the other needed for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in order to help stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It said the U.S. dollar borrowing would be backed by U.S. government securities as collateral. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the agreement was similar to earlier repo pacts it signed with Japan, Malaysia, Indonesia, Australia, Hong Kong, Singapore and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  It did not reveal the ceiling of U.S. dollar borrowing provided by the agreement but said earlier that each bilateral pact has a $500 million limit. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier this month when the Thai baht came under heavy attacks. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662)-6520642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5r04w62\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
