\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Computer Breakdown/SET -3: Reality Not Clear \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1997\par 14:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The reality on Monday wasn't so clear cut as some investors would have hoped. Instead of cutting the discount rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was changing the way the minimum retail rate is calculated. This means the MRR will be freed up from bank deposit rates, a Bank of Thailand spokeswoman said, allowing the retail rate to move independently from the prime rate. \par \par \uc2  But there's one exception. The retail rate won't be allowed to rise more than 4 percentage points over the prime rate, which stands at 13% in Thailand. Analysts said the move allows banks to charge their retail clients more, freeing up funds to ease rates to commercial borrowers. \par \par \uc2  A dim signal it may have been, but it was enough to spark some reaction among leading commercial banks. 'There was some good news out there,' said Songyos Kulvichien, first vice president at Securities One PCL. 'Thai Farmers Bank cut its minimum lending rate, and this could spark some buying.' \par \par \uc2  Thai Farmers Bank PCL (P.TFB) reduced its minimum lending rate by 25 basis points to 12.75%. Bangkok Bank PCL (P.BBK), the country's largest, was fast on its heels, announcing a planned minimum lending rate cut of 25 basis points to 12.75% this week too. \par \par \uc2  'I think we'll have to cut the rate within this week. Other banks are doing this too,' said Executive Vice President Piti Sithi-Amnuai. He said Bangkok Bank's minimum lending rate would to fall 25 basis points to 12.75%. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy move could suggest difficulties in getting interest rates down further, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  'They're trying to bring the rates down without affecting the baht,' said Sriyan Pietersz, market strategist at Capital Nomura Securites PCL. He said it would be difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring rates down further because of the need to protect the baht from further attacks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Last week, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  successfully fended off an attack from speculators through massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1203GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 62559 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5q03wfd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
