\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Lower Early As Dollar-Buying Mounts \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1997\par 04:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is dropping against the dollar in early Asian trading Thursday, as investors began buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it rose against the Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also weakening in the swap market, although the swap rates remain unusually high. Swap rates are dropping as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped increase money supply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the U.S. dollar is at 25.765 baht, up from 25.730 baht at the close of trading Wednesday. At that level, the dollar is trading close to the upper limit of the band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows it to trade against the baht, indicating rising demand for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand, fixing its daily midrate for the dollar at 25.75 baht Thursday, set its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band between 25.73 baht and 25.77 baht. The dollar midrate was 25.71 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors are buying dollars following its early rise against the Japanese yen. 'It's just moving in line with the midrate, which is higher than yesterday,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar, the yen and the Deustche mark. Because of the peg, the baht tends to weaken when the dollar rises against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates are as follows, in satang (100 satang equals 1 baht).\par       Thursday    Wednesday   Monday      Friday\par 1 mo  45.0-70.0   60.0-75.0   75.0-90.0   35.0-45.0\par 2 mo  80.0-105.0  70.0-90.0   70.0-100.0  45.0-50.0\par 3 mo  90.0-115.0  105.0-125.0 80.0-110.0  55.0-90.0\par 6 mo  110.0-150.0 140.0-170.0 125.0-160.0 60.0-100.0\par 1 yr  170.0-220.0 200.0-240.0 160.0-190.0 105.0-135.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0241GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5m03r25\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
