\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Lower As Dollar Rebounds Against Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1997\par 13:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht fell against the dollar in Asian spot trading Thursday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded against the Japanese yen after Wednesday's decline, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said trading was quiet as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's orders not to sell baht to offshore investors remained in place. 'Offshore investors make up a large part of the market, and without them, trading is quiet,' one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future, the baht strengthened slightly. Swap rates on baht fell. \par \par \uc2  At the close of spot trading, the dollar rose to 25.805 baht from Wednesday's close of 25.730 baht. At that rate, the baht was outside the band in which the Bank of Thailand allows it to trade freely against the dollar. When the baht falls outside the band - set at 25.73 baht to 25.77 baht Thursday - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Dealers, though, said they were unaware of any such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its dollar-baht midrate at 25.75 baht to the dollar Thursday, compared with 25.71 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed against the baht on the back of its rebound against the Japanese yen. The Thai baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the dollar, the yen and the German mark. When the dollar advances against its major counterparts, the baht tends to weaken. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was inactive because the Bank of Thailand's orders to commercial banks not to sell baht to offshore investors were still in place. The instructions were issued to punish speculators after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged to a seven-year low of 26.30 baht against the dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1105GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5m03p2o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
