\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Higher, Central Bk Order Remains In Place \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 1997\par 12:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended higher against the dollar in Asian spot trading Wednesday as Thai commercial banks continued to obey the instruction by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to sell baht to offshore investors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Because of that, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also generally stronger in the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Long-term swap rates rose as shrinking money supply helped prop up the cost of forward trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 25.730 baht, down from 25.850 baht Monday. Thai financial markets were closed Tuesday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, the dollar was trading within the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, indicating little \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fixing the midrate at 25.71 baht Wednesday, allowed the dollar to move within the band of 25.69 baht and 25.73 baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was mixed with foreign investors rushing to buy baht back, moving to meet their previous agreements to sell baht in favor of dollars. Meanwhile, Thai commercial banks which have been holding onto their baht following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's instruction began seeking dollars to cover their short positions. \par \par \uc2  Moving to punish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators who launched last week a new round of attack against the baht, the Bank of Thailand has asked Thai banks to add a 1,000% premium to its lending to foreign banks seeking baht for their settlements in the spot market. Though the bank declared that speculation is over, commercial banks said the order for such a high premium and the halt of baht selling hasn't been revoked. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1050GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5l03nh3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
