\par\par \b \uc2  S.E. Asia Central Bks/Baht -2: Tighter Monetary Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 14:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand was joined by the other members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) in supporting the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said early Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore described the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as 'effective'. \par \par \uc2  But the sources said the coup de grace of the banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the squeeze in short term interest rates engineered Thursday and Friday in Thailand, Malaysia and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  'I'm less impressed with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more impressed with the rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rates,' said the senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a U.S. investment bank, speaking on condition of anonymity. '(The Bank of Thailand) dried up liquidity to punish the speculators,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Overt measures by the Bank of Thailand - urging domestic banks not to lend baht to offshore counterparties at rates less then 1,000% - ensured that many speculators who wanted to liquidate short positions in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do so only at an unacceptable cost. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara has also pushed up short-term interest rates to defend the ringgit, though it was quick to deny suggestions Friday that it was penalizing offshore players in the ringgit swaps market. Bank Indonesia issued a similar denial Friday. \par \par \uc2  And the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jacked up its overnight interest rates in stages to 20% by Friday from 12% Wednesday, steadying the Philippine peso by the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing rooms were frantic Friday as liquidity in the forward and swap markets evaporated. \par \par \uc2  'The (local) banks were quoting such ridiculous spreads... basically Thailand and Malaysia were barricading their capital accounts (from offshore players),' said Chia Wooh Khien, treasury economist at Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken (South East Asia) Ltd. in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The sources agreed the effect of sharply higher short-term interest rates in Malaysia and Thailand had much the same effect Friday as a temporary imposition of exchange controls. 'This hasn't been a natural market,' said StanChart's Van der Wath. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1229GMT \par \par \uc2  1148 4201 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03ifn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
