\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht/Late -2: Some Worry Of Renewed Attack Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 13:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'They have to pay the price,' Chaiyawat said. But those rates would apply only to foreign speculators, who can be identified because Thai banks kept records of who sold baht this week, he said. \par \par \uc2  By late Friday, however, interbank rates were slumping. The overnight and call interbank rates were quoted at 15% to 16%, down from 18%. A key swap rate, the tommorrow/next rate, was down to 0.001 baht, down from 1 baht early Friday. At its morning level, the 'tom/next' rate implied an annual interest of 1,431% - which stifled baht speculation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates were as follows, in satang (100 satang equals 1 baht).\par      Friday        Thursday     Wednesday   Tuesday\par 1 mo 35.0-45.0     100.0-130.0  23.0-26.0   6.75-7.25\par 2 mo 45.0-50.0     130.0-170.0  35.0-39.0   12.75-13.5\par 3 mo 55.0-90.0     130.0-140.0  45.0-50.0   19.0-19.25\par 6 mo 60.0-100.0    160.0-185.0  67.0-69.0   38.0-38.5\par 1 yr 1.05-1.35     190.0-220.0  110-115.0   77.0-79.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the drop in rates indicated that speculators had indeed\par been beaten back. But many said that despite the massive show of force\par by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which was joined in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, the threat of a fresh attack remains\par strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 'If interest rates come down, maybe the market will start buying\par dollars again on Monday,' a dealer at a U.S. bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's fixed-exchange rate system, analysts say, has become an\par awkward and obsolete monetary tool as the economy has matured. As long\par as it endures, they said, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will attract speculators whose\par determination to break the system will grow with each attack.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1138GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03i1a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
