\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Shares End Higher On Stock Support Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 12:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--Thai stock prices finished higher Friday as selling pressure eased following a wire service report that the government will announce new measures to pick up the free-falling stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After five straight sessions of losses, the Stock Exchange of Thailand index closed 3.32 points higher at 561.19 points, from Thursday's closing of 557.87 points Thursday. About 176.5 million shares valued at 4.71 billion baht changed hands, compared with 221.8 million shares at 6.63 billion baht Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Advancers outnumbered decliners 159 to 135, excluding foreign shares. At the close of Friday's session, the SET index was 33% down on its 1996 year-end close of 831.57. The SET 50 index, comprising the 50 most actively traded stocks, closed up 0.26 point at 40.66. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors reduced their selling late in the afternoon session following a wire service report that the government will on Monday introduce new measures to support the stock market. The report, however, didn't specify what the new measures will be. \par \par \uc2  'Many investors stopped selling on the report just to see what's going to happen next,' said an analyst at Asia Credit PCL. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many investors also took a break from selling as the recent speculative attack against the Thai baht tailed off. \par \par \uc2  Since Wednesday, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hurt by rumors that it will be devalued. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has flatly denied the rumors and moved to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets both at home and abroad to perk up the baht. On Friday, a top \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official declared that there was no more speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1016GMT \par \par \uc2  5048 55107 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03him\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
