\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Dlr/Baht -3: Swap Rates Surge \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 04:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht slumped to its lowest level in more than seven years Wednesday amid a new round of speculative attack caused by fears of devaluation. The attack, which dealers said was as severe as the one in late January and early February, also caused Thai stock prices to fall to a new six-and-a-half-year low, pushed the interbank rates to a three-month high and drove swap rates up sharply. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment toward the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained negative Thursday amid uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to maintain its fixed exchange-rate policy, dealers said. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , moving to defend the baht, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  both in offshore markets and at home. However, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to help the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with selling pressure coming from all directions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't moved to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market in early Thursday trading, said a dealer at a Japanese bank in Bangkok. However, the current spot rate may prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shortly. At 0211 GMT (10:11 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at 25.910 baht, below its Wednesday's level but well outside the Bank of Thailand's limit. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates, meanwhile, are also surging - a result of vigorous demand\par for dollars in the future coupled with tight money supply, dealers said.\par Swap rates are as follows, in satang (100 satang equals 1 baht). The\par rates were the highest since February.\par        Thursday    Wednesday   Tuesday     Monday\par 1 mo   60.0-65.0   23.0-26.0   6.75-7.25   6.0-6.25\par 2 mo   80.0-85.0   35.0-39.0   12.75-13.5  11.75-12.0\par 3 mo   80.0-90.0   45.0-50.0   19.0-19.25  17.75-18.25\par 6 mo   125.0-135.0 67.0-69.0   38.0-38.5   35.5-36.5\par 1 yr   195.0-215.0 110-115.0   77.0-79.0   73.5-75.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0233GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03jvc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
