\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Fin Min/Baht -3: Thai Banks Stopped Trading Baht \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 20:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Six countries have non-binding agreements with Thailand to help the country in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crises, but only Singapore so far has openly come to Thailand's assistance. Amnuay, however, said that all other SEACEN central banks joined in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He also said Japan confirmed to \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  its willingness to help defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay spoke at a press conference upon his return from a visit to Japan. He said the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Southeast Asian central banks had so stung speculators that no additional defenses were needed. The baht closed at a six-month high as the dollar slumped to 25.40 baht from 26.30 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  As the attack on the baht began Wednesday, some economists speculated that Thailand may impose controls on the flow of short-term capital in and out of the country to stabilize the baht. That would mean following a precedent set by Malaysia during a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis a few years ago. But Amnuay said 'It's not necessary.' \par \par \uc2  Thailand's defense against the attack took also took the form of public-private-sector cooperation, Amnuay said. He said Thai banks voluntarily decided to stop trading baht with foreign banks, thus shrinking the supply of available \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for speculators to use. \par \par \uc2  'Today commercial banks did not sell or lend baht,' Amnuay said. 'When you don't sell the baht, there's no supply for commercial banks to use to speculate any further.' He denied the banks had been asked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop trading the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian central banks would have had ample reason to help Thailand defend the baht Thursday. The baht crisis sent shudders through financial markets in Malaysia, Indonesia and the Philippines, causing stock prices to tumble there. On Wednesday, it triggered a sell-off in the Malaysian and Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1833GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03j2h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
