\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 /Baht/Amplifier -2: More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely Fri \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 16:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars for baht, but made no comment on the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also declined to say whether other central banks had come to its aid, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore did Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A top aide to Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh said \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  would ask Japan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defense of the baht. The Bank of Japan made no public comment on whether it had been asked to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in behalf of the baht. But a senior BOJ official said the BOJ was 'relieved' by the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement Thursday and is watching policy developments in Thailand. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  achieved Thursday what it failed to Wednesday as it dramatically beat back speculators. Despite big \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Thai and Singaporean banks Wednesday, the dollar finished the day at 26.30 baht, 0.42 baht outside the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band - the biggest deviation from the band in more than a year. \par \par \uc2  By mid-day Thursday, however, the defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had turned from a fight to keep the baht from depreciating to a fight to keep it from appreciating. The dollar swung outside the lower limit of the trading band, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was actually buying dollars to keep the baht down. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 25.40 baht, its lowest level since Nov. 20, and 0.39 baht outside the lower limit of the range. That implies the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to continue buying dollars Friday to stabilize the baht. \par \par \uc2  'I'm very concerned about this,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at the Bank of Thailand. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading range for the dollar Thursday was 25.79 baht to 25.83 baht. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1420GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03hr4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
