\par\par \b \uc2  S.E. Asia Mkts/Baht -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen Key Factor \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 13:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'There are big differences (between) what's happening in Thailand and what happened in Mexico, and I'm not in the least in fear that things will spill over from Thailand as they did from Mexico,' said Hans Beck, Asia-Pacific chief executive of investment bank Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. \par \par \uc2  Southeast Asian countries, all armed with large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, are enjoying robust, although in some cases, slowing economic growth. That applies even to Thailand, market sources pointed out. \par \par \uc2  In any case, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declared victory Thursday over the speculators - for the moment at least - with the baht strengthening against the U.S. dollar to a six-month high in the spot market. A Bank of Thailand official told Dow Jones that speculators have 'given up' their attempt to push the baht down. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended the Asian trading day at 25.400 baht, outside the lower end of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 25.79 to 25.83 baht \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which obliges the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars at below market rates. The dollar had started the day outside the higher end of the band. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that a key factor likely to shore up sentiment in the region is the coordinated effort by the region's central banks to ward off the speculators. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Monetary Aurthority of Singapore said they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  together Wednesday to support the baht, with unconfirmed reports that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Malaysia's Bank Negara did so too. \par \par \uc2  'The public acknowledgement of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is important,' said Hatheway. 'A country like Singapore has medium and longer term interests in fostering (southeast Asian) cooperation and stability,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Several fund managers said the MAS's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals the importance the central banks assign to maintaining stability in regional financial markets. The central banks, which signed a web of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection agreements in the past two years, would lose credibility if the baht is devalued, they said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1153GMT \par \par \uc2  1142 4201 62550 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03gtv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
