\par\par \b \uc2  Japan BOJ/Baht -2: Remarks Made Amid Baht Volatility \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan has no comment on whether the government of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has approached Japan with a request to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the baht, a senior Bank of Japan official said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking on condition of anonymity, the official also denied an earlier report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had suggested such a request was made. Earlier Thursday, one foreign newswire in Tokyo reported that a BOJ official confirmed such a request had been made. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ official said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 'relieved' over the baht's movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday and said 'It looks like market sentiment regarding the baht is stabilizing, even improving already.' \par \par \uc2  After a sharp selloff earlier, the Thai baht rose amid \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  baht buying in Bangkok and Singapore Thursday. The baht had plunged to a seven-year low Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is currently quoted at 25.30 baht. \par \par \uc2  The official said the Bank of Japan is currently taking a wait-and-see stance and closely watching further steps on economic and financial policy that may be taken by the Thai government. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the BOJ and the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain in close contact. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Thursday, a Thai official said Thailand will seek Japanese assistance to combat a speculative attack on the baht. \par \par \uc2  'We will ask our major trading partners, like Singapore and Japan, to spend some money to defend the baht,' Poosana Premanoch, Chavalit's deputy secretary-general told reporters. Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht in concert with the Bank of Thailand. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03gje\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
