\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Shares Lower At Midday; SET Down 4.2% Or 23.99 Pts \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 07:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai stock market's main barometer is 4.2% lower midday Thursday as investors bail out of the market amid continued selling of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on concern over the health of the economy, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  At 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the Stock Exchange of Thailand index is down 23.99 points to 547.31, after ranging from a high of 565.52 and a low of 544.10 points. \par \par \uc2  The SET 50 Index is 2.08 points lower at 39.54. \par \par \uc2  At midday, declining shares outnumber advances 268 to 31 on trading volume of 84.4 million shares worth 2.89 billion baht. \par \par \uc2  'Sentiment in the stock market is very bad,' one dealer said. 'There's a lot of pressure still weighing on the baht, and there's a lot of uncertainty about what will happen.' \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht suffered more selling in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday morning after it sank to a low of 26.25 baht to the dollar Thursday. But by midday, the baht was stabilizing after reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas markets. At 0534 GMT (1:34 a.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at 25.70 baht. \par \par \uc2  The selling was sparked by concerns over the Thai government's ability to handle the country's slowing economy. \par \par \uc2  But despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the anxious mood at the SET isn't lifting. Dealers said investors were selling across the board, and foreigners were dumping blue-chip stocks. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok Bank PCL is 7 baht lower at 149, with Thai Farmers Bank PCL down 2.50 baht to 97.50. Advanced Info Service PCL is 1 baht down at 154, with industrial conglomerate Siam Cement PCL 54 baht lower at 504. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0558GMT \par \par \uc2  5048 55107 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03dlc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
