\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht rallies late as rates hit speculators. \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 15 (Reuter) - The Thai baht rallied in late trade on Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed banks to quote Friday for Monday delivery deals for overseas clients at high financing costs, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The high baht rates foiled speculators, severely tightened liquidity and renewed interest in the baht, they added. \par \par \uc2  The baht strengthened to 25.300/25.340 per dollar at 1022 GMT from 25.910/25.940 early, dealers said. The Bank of Thailand fixed the mid-rate at 25.81 a dollar against 25.85 on Wednesday. "The spot market was quite calm down today with more dollar being offered in the market," said a dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand stressed on Thursday it would maintain high interest rates to defend against speculative attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The offshore players also found it difficult to borrow funds for speculation in the baht as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was earlier said to inform banks in Thailand not quote to offshore parties for tom/next activities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the afternoon allowed banks to resume quoting tom/next to non-resident clients. \par \par \uc2  "We are allowed to resume quoting tom/next (for Friday dollar/baht deals and Monday delivery) for overseas clients but at about two baht," said one broker at a foreign bank. said. \par \par \uc2  The authorities made it clear that local banks would have to offer funds at high financing costs to discourage speculation against the baht, she added. \par \par \uc2  Most players were also wary of pushing the baht down further amid worries about another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its regional counterparts to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Singapore on Wednesday jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Singapore market to stabilise the battered baht. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said on Thursday it may join hands with other Asian central banks and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to help support the baht if asked to do so by Thailand. \par \par \uc2  But forward premiums were shooting up further due to a severe shortage of funds after recent buying of the dollar by speculators, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The one-month baht/dollar swap premium jumped to 15.00/16.00 satangs per dollar late from 12.00/13.00 in early morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate eased to 14.00-15.00 percent late from 18.00-20.00 percent early, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Most banks had done nothing today. But I heard the rate of 14.00-15.00 was being done in the market in the afternoon," said one money market dealer. \par \par \uc2  -- Anuchit Nguyen (662) 652-0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05nui\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
