\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ may help support Thai baht, but not yet - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elaine Lies \par \uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 15 (Reuter) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it may join hands with other Asian central banks and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to help support the crumbling Thai baht if asked to do so by Thailand. \par \par \uc2  Any such moves would be part of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  safety net agreement reached between Asian monetary authorities in 1996, an official at the Bank of Japan (BOJ) told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The agreement is there, although it is not a thing we would activate unless we were asked by Thailand," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We have an agreement, and if we want to use it, we certainly will. But it's not a question of our making the first move," he added. \par \par \uc2  Last year, Japan agreed with the monetary authorities of Australia, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand to establish bilateral repurchase agreements to provide liquidity in times of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Such "repo" pacts give participants instant access to cash -- for use to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against excessive volatility -- by virtue of them selling their holdings in U.S. government securities to partners with a promise to buy them back later. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, in the first use of this agreement, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also said to have bought the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it fell to 26.250-26.300 to the dollar, though there was no confirmation. \par \par \uc2  Rising concerns about the slowing Thai economy and rumours of political turmoil in the cabinet that could lead to the possible resignation of Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan triggered heavy baht sales for the dollar on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay, who has repeatedly denied he will quit, reiterated on Thursday that Thailand will defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against attacks in the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. \par \par \uc2  "We have been successful and we will be successful," he said, adding: "We have support from all our friends." \par \par \uc2  But Tokyo dealers said it may well take time before the BOJ joins any future moves, saying the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main concern at this point is the dollar's volatile moves against the yen. The greenback has plunged more than 10 yen in the past two weeks, and some fear even more slides lie ahead. \par \par \uc2  "Right now the BOJ has its hands completely full just trying to deal with the dollar and yen. This isn't the time for it to think about other things," said one Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a major Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  He said, and others agreed, that if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did agree to take part in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the impact definitely would be stronger. \par \par \uc2  "But they would have to be very careful how they did it because to see the BOJ selling dollars, even against an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , risks sending a strange signal to the market and could accelerate the dollar's fall against the yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a long-term credit bank, citing the weak Thai economy, said he was concerned by the possibility that not all of Wednesday's sales were speculative. \par \par \uc2  "There's the worry that the flow of capital out of the country may be starting to pick up speed, meaning the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation could drag on for a long time and diminish the impact of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  But most dealers said they felt it was unlikely the BOJ would refrain from taking part in future joint moves should the baht depreciate seriously, owing to the need to maintain favourable ties among other Asian nations and its huge financial involvement in the region. \par \par \uc2  "Totally aside from the question of its investment in Thailand, which of course is one concern, Japan has made a big deal about its cooperative ties with other Asian nations. So if the baht falls further, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  asks it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they will most likely take part," the credit-bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05nrx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
