\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Thai baht adjustment inevitable, analysts say. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Koetsawang \par \uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 08:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 15 (Reuter) - Reform of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system is inevitable after this week's stinging speculator attacks on the baht, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But they ruled out devaluation as a way of appeasing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  predators, saying it was likely to result in more grief than joy for the government and economy. \par \par \uc2  "The fixed exchanged rate, capital mobility and effective monetary policy cannot coexist," said an analyst from a U.S. brokerage firm. \par \par \uc2  "It is not the question of whether the Bank of Thailand has enough resources to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I'm sure it does. But why allow the inflexible baht to be a constant irritation to the monetary policy?" \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Thailand could not afford to allow interest rates to come down in order to boost the sagging economy -- projected by private analysts to grow at a decade-low of less than six percent this year -- without letting go of the baht. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts declined to speculate on a time frame for any adjustment but some felt it could happen in six to 12 months. \par \par \uc2  Offshore speculators attacked the baht this week despite its high-yielding rates, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to swing widely out of the four-satang band within which the Bank of Thailand now allows it to fluctuate. \par \par \uc2  The attacks forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the market along with other regional central banks and issue repeated denials of a devaluation or any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustment. \par \par \uc2  The baht is now pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is confidential, but believed to heavily weight the dollar. The dollar's weight was increased to about 80 percent in 1986 when it was clear that the dollar was trending down at a rapid pace, economists said. \par \par \uc2  The basket peg was suitable for Thailand during 1985-1995 as a long decline in the dollar kept the baht undervalued and Thai exports competitive, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The system also made the baht one of the most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region and an easy target for interest rate arbitraging. \par \par \uc2  But the peg also attracted speculative attacks on the baht when the dollar jumped in February, resulting in considerable disruption in the domestic money market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand has kept interest rates high to defend the baht against attacks, but this week its strategy came under pressure again as more attacks set in. \par \par \uc2  "If you allowed the baht to reflect market sentiment by making it more flexible, then you don't have to worry about interest rates," said Song Seng Wun of ABN-AMRO Hoare Govett in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the baht and pushed up the implied overnight interbank rate to punish speculators. The action did calm the market somewhat on Thursday as the baht was quoted at 25.790-25.890 against 26.330-26.430 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "There's blood on the streets. The speculators are being burned," said the head of trading at a European bank of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Chia Woon Khien, regional economist of Singapore-based Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken, speculated that the Bank of Thailand was likely to adjust the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  first. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do so by gradually reducing the weight of the strengthening dollar in the basket and widening the trading band later when economic conditions stabilised. \par \par \uc2  "Between a re-balancing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket and a widening of the trading band, the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is likely to adopt the former first, given that the first is more discretionary and reversible," she said. \par \par \uc2  But the timing for any such adjustment was crucial, said Supavud Saicheua of Phatra Reseach. \par \par \uc2  A belief that the dollar was on the rise, concern about poor Thai export prospects and a still large current account deficit would be compelling reasons for people to believe that a more flexible baht could result in a weaker baht, he added. \par \par \uc2  "But we believe that a more flexible baht need not imply short-term disruption or induce damaging speculation if appropriately timed," he said in a report. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05ngk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
