\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Thai  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  firms after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deborah Charles \par \uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 15 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  successfully defended its embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a squeeze on liquidity and reassurances that there were no plans to devalue. \par \par \uc2  Several Asian central banks cooperated with \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  by jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the embattled baht against speculative attacks, Thai deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi said. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted sharply firmer at 25.250/25.350 late on Thursday against 25.910/25.940 early in the morning and 26.330/26.430 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to ask the private sector to have confidence in the government policy and not to listen to the rumours," the Bank of Thailand said earlier in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wishes to stress that there would be no devaluation or changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange mechanism which were mentioned by rumours," it said. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, dealers said the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had ordered local banks not to quote tomorrow/next rates in the baht to offshore parties, effectively cutting off a source of short-term borrowing to fund speculation. \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan on Thursday also repeated the government's determination to guard the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculative attacks. He said in Tokyo the government's defence of the baht has been, and will be, successful. \par \par \uc2  Rising concerns about the slowing Thai economy and rumours of political turmoil in the cabinet that could lead to Amnuay's possible resignation triggered heavy baht sales for the dollar on Wednesday. Amnuay has repeatedly denied he would quit. \par \par \uc2  "(On Wednesday) there was fierce speculation on the baht in the overseas market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said. "At present the situation has eased to a certain degree." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to defend the baht. Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trade sources said, although their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not confirmed. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said on Thursday that, if asked, it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help support the baht under a 1996 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  safety net agreement. \par \par \uc2  Last year monetary authorities of Australia, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand agreed to establish bilateral repurchase agreements to provide liquidity in times of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay said that Thailand has support "from all our friends" in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  defence. He also moved to soothe fears about the deterioration in the Thai economy, saying the country was "in a process of recovery." \par \par \uc2  The economy had gone through its worst, he said, adding he was pleased with a sharp decline in the current account deficit and inflation, and expectations that exports were improving. \par \par \uc2  The market rumours also hit the Thai bourse on Thursday, causing the market to drop to near eight-year lows. The main index closed at 557.87 points, a fall of 2.35 percent. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  woes have unnerved other markets in the region with the Philippine peso, the Malaysian ringgit and the Indonesian rupiah also suffering heavy selling. \par \par \uc2  The statement, which came after heavy speculative attacks on the baht this week and a plunge in the stock market index to near eight-year-lows, said the premier's office also provided reassurance that the Thai economic situation remained stable. \par \par \uc2  To fight baht speculators, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local and foreign markets, especially on Wednesday when the run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  heightened. \par \par \uc2  It also sought assistance from regional counterparts to fight speculators and received support from them, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. \par \par \uc2  The statemet said inflation had decreased from seven percent last year to 4.4 percent and the forecasted current account deficit was expected to be six percent of gross domestic product at the end of this year compared to over eight percent last year, it added. \par \par \uc2  The structure of the long term debt had risen to 60 percent from 50 percent, it added. \par \par \uc2  "Next week Mr. Amnuay Viravan and the Governor of the Bank of Thailand are also preparing to announce additional measures to promote confidence in the Thai economy and financial institutions as well as measures to increase its liquidity," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  "As a result there are no reasons whatsoever to devalue the baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it added. \par \par \uc2  The baht rallied late on Thursday supported by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was quoted at 25.300/400 against the dollar compared with 26.330/430 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05n72\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
