\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Thai stocks at eight-year-low but jitters ease. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deborah Charles \par \uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 15 (Reuter) - The Thai bourse suffered more losses to approach new eight-year lows on Thursday but analysts said the mood was less frantic as the baht stabilised and fears of an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalution eased. \par \par \uc2  After nearly three weeks of declines, the battered Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) key index shed another 2.35 percent to close at 557.87 points -- the lowest finish since May 1989. \par \par \uc2  The market had dropped as low as 544.10 before late fund buying pared losses, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  Talk of a possible baht devaluation over the past few days had battered the stock market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the baht rallied late on Thursday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assurances by Thai authorities that it would not devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 25.350/25.450 to the dollar in late dealings, compared with 26.330/26.430 late on Wednesday when it was hammered by speculators. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand on Thursday reassured investors it had no plans to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wishes to stress that there would be no devaluation or changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange mechanism which were mentioned by rumours," it said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan also repeated the government's determination to guard the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculative attacks. He said the government's defence of the baht has been, and will be, successful. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the reassurances and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other central banks helped stabilise the baht and, in turn, the stock market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday, and other regional central banks were said to have done the same, although it was not confirmed. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan said it would be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht if asked to do so. \par \par \uc2  "We had believed that the baht was not going to be devalued," said David Riedel, vice president of research for Salomon Brothers. "This latest attack has been beaten back." \par \par \uc2  But he said the latest assault on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the third in six months and it could lead investors to be wary of investing too heavily in baht. \par \par \uc2  "I think investors are... wary of a resurgence. They have to watch it very carefully," he said. \par \par \uc2  Stock traders said local funds were encouraged by renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability and the pledge of support from the Bank of Japan, so they went bargain-hunting in afternoon dealings. \par \par \uc2  Many foreign investors, spooked by Wednesday's heavy speculative assault on the baht and worried about the underlying weakness of the Thai economy, unloaded blue chips throughout the day, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The market has been battered lately not only by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also by worries over the slowing economy, lacklustre first quarter earnings and troubled finance and propery sectors. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05n3n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
