\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand to fight  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  speculation -- Amnuay. \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 15 (Reuter) - Thailand will defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against attacks in the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We are determined to fight speculation," Amnuay told an international conference on Asia, in response to a question about speculative moves in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Singapore market to stabilise the baht after the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to 26.250-26.300 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay also told the conference that the Thai economy is in a process of recovery. \par \par \uc2  "We are in a process of recovery," he said. "We are through the worst, but there is much left to do," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Thai economy is in its worst shape in 10 years, with gross domestic product projected to expand about five to six percent this year, after 6.7 percent in 1996 and 8.6 percent in 1995. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay also dismissed questions about a possible devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "That's a silly question," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability was due partly to dollar/yen fluctuations and partly to speculators trying to take advantage of such moves. \par \par \uc2  "We are determined to fight speculation. I repeat we are determined to fight speculation," he said. \par \par \uc2  Referring to the Thai economy, he said the economy had gone through its worst, but much was still to be done. "You can't solve economic ills in a few weeks or months." \par \par \uc2  He said he was pleased with many economic indicators, especially the drastic decline in the current account deficit and the decline in inflation, adding that exports looked to be improving. \par \par \uc2  "We have had some financial sector problems that would make the recovery process perhaps slow," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We believe some measures we have launched have had some positive effects and we will be able to resolve the problems in the near future." \par \par \uc2  Asked about regional financial cooperation, he said: "Concerted action on the part of member countries in the region will be needed because of the magnitude of the flow of funds in the region." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05mmy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
