\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand Currency \highlight\uc2 /Amplifier -4:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen As Weak \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par 16:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  To shore up its defenses of the baht, Thailand in the last year has been signing agreements with the central banks of several countries. It has \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -cooperation agreements with Australia, Hong Kong, Singapore, Malaysia, the Philippines and Japan. As of Wednesday, however, only Singapore had openly come to Thailand's defense. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore made no comment on its decision beyond a joint statement released with the Bank of Thailand. That statement said: 'This concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at stemming excessive speculative activities, which may lead to disorderly conditions in the Thai and regional financial markets. Other appropriate measures will be taken as necessary.' \par \par \uc2  The attack on the baht also sparked a sell-off in the Malysian ringgit and the Indonesian rupiah Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Singapore said the authority's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been modest. 'We're not sure how much the authorities bought but the way the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being done doesn't seem to be effective,' said the chief of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a Japanese bank in Singapore. 'It seems the market is having the upper hand.' \par \par \uc2  If the market continues to enjoy the upper hand over several days, many analysts said, Thailand could be forced to submit to a policy change. Thailand's foreign reserves - $38.1 billion in March - are ample, but experts say a sustained attack could drain even that amount. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 'From a pure fundamental point of view, there's no need for Thailand\par to do something immediately on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,' said Bernhard Eschweiler,\par an economist with J.P. Morgan Inc. in Singapore. 'But from a market\par point of view Thailand is clearly vulnerable.' Wednesday's attack on the\par baht, he said, amounted to 'a big bang on the door' by speculators who\par smell blood.\par    -Joseph Rajendran in Singapore contributed to this article.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-05-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1435GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5e03hcv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
