\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Frailty Shows In Baht Attack -Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Joseph Rebello and James Hookway \par \uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par 15:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--Jolted by an attack on the baht that sent shudders through other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday, Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  received aid from Singapore for the first time in defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The attack on the baht, in which foreign institutional investors dumped baht for dollars to test Thailand's bank's ability to maintain its fixed exchange-rate system, pushed the dollar to its highest level in more than seven years against the baht. \par \par \uc2  In the panic that followed, Thai stock prices plunged to a six-and-a-half-year low as the benchmark Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) index fell 28.94 points to 571.30. Interbank rates surged to 20%, a three-month high. Swap rates soared. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand, scrambling to defend a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system that has been the foundation of Thai economic policy for 13 years, found succor in an unusual quarter. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, usually loath to enter the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggles of other countries, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said it was the first time the two banks had acted in concert. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was less successful than previous attempts to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - a sign, analysts said, not only of Thailand's reduced economic circumstances, but also of the growing difficulty of keeping the baht pegged to a dollar-dominated basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar closed at 26.30 baht - 0.42 baht outside the upper limit of the band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows it to trade versus the baht. The dollar Tuesday closed at 25.915 baht. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1346GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5e03h30\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
