\par\par \b \uc2  Baht hit by finance portfolio rumour, economy woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vithoon Amorn \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par 13:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 14 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to defend the baht against fresh market attacks, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned of taking more actions to counter market pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it teamed up with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Singapore market to stabilise the baht. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first joint action confirmed by the two central banks, came after the baht fell to 26.250-26.300 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered to 26.030-26.080 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, but it was quoted sharply weaker at 26.550-26.750 during off-hour trading late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know if the baht would see a calmer market tomorrow. It still looks weak and fragile after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  But another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Thai Military Bank Plc said she expected speculators to lie low on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed its determination to back the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said: "This concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at stemming excessive speculative activities which may lead to disorderly conditions in the Thai and regional financial markets. Other appropriate measures will be taken as necessary." \par \par \uc2  The baht's woes were partly triggered by suggestions last weekend by members in Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh's coalition for Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan to resign and take responsibility for Thailand's mounting economic problems. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay told Reuters in Tokyo, after attending a meeting of the Asian Development Bank in the Japanese city of Fukuoka, that he was confident of his future as finance minister. \par \par \uc2  He said Thailand was committed to maintaining baht stability and its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would succeed in turning back any further market attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chavalit on Tuesday voiced his full backing for Amnuay. The prime minister also ruled out any plan to devalue the baht. \par \par \uc2  The Thai economy is in its worst shape in 10 years with gross domestic product projected to expand about five to six percent, against 6.7 percent in 1996 and 8.6 percent in 1995. \par \par \uc2  The attacks on the baht sent more shock waves through the ailing stock market, where the Composite Index plunged 4.82 percent to a near eight-year low of 571.30 points on Wednesday. The index has lost 13.6 percent this month. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministry officials and some private bankers said the damage from a baht devaluation would outweigh benefits for the Thai economy. \par \par \uc2  They said a devaluation would not substantially help Thai exports as more than 75 percent were industrial products with high import contents. The officials said a devalued baht would instead sharply raise the financing costs of Thailand's estimated $90 billion foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  "Efforts to dampen speculation on Amnuay's future were not helped by his absence," a dealer at Hongkong and Shanghai Bank said. Amnuay is not due back in Bangkok until Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Siri Ganjarerndee attributed the attack on the baht to negative market perception of the Thai economy and to rumours of possible economic policy and finance portfolio changes. \par \par \uc2  He told reporters the rumours prompted a market flight to the dollar from baht, a move sharply tightening short-term domestic liquidity. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5e05krn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
