\par\par \b \uc2  Dealers suspect BOT  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  on heavy baht sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 14 (Reuter) - Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said they believed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht in the Singapore market during midday Wednesday but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not confirm it. \par \par \uc2  They said the market saw heavy selling offers on baht, mostly from Singapore dealers shortly before noon, on renewed jitters over Thai economic policies and speculation about a possible change in the Thai finance portfolio. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment whether the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The baht fell to 26.250-26.300 to the dollar before it recovered to 26.030-26.080 at 0656 GMT. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the baht/dollar midrate at 25.86 on Wednesday against 25.88 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "I heard that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , otherwise the baht could not stage such a comeback," a Thai bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said their Singapore counterparts quoted baht selling offers in big $100 million lots against $10-30 million deals in normal market conditions. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment was weak this morning and the market just reacted to a combination of negative factors. Economic indicators showed no signs of improvement, the stock market tumbled and the market speculated on whether there would be any economic policy changes," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai stock market index tumbled by the Wednesday lunch break to its lowest level since mid-June 1989. \par \par \uc2  Stock and money markets have been concerned in the past few days by suggestions by some members in Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh's government that a change in the finance portfolio could help shore up market confidence. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay, who is attending a meeting of the Asian Development Bank in Japan, has not indicated that he would step down. \par \par \uc2  The Thai economy is in its worst shape in a decade with the gross domestic product projected to expand at about five to six percent this year against 6.7 in 1996 and 8.6 in 1995. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662)-6520642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5e05kgl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
