\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Ends Dn; Uncertainty Over Fin Min's Future \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 1997\par 13:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht fell against the dollar in Asian spot trading Tuesday as investors dumped the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on growing fears the country's finance minister may be replaced, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums rose as a result of brisk dollar-buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Tuesday, the dollar was at 25.915 baht, up from 25.910 baht on Monday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, the dollar was well outside the band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the dollar to move against the baht Tuesday, reflecting strong market demand for dollars. The band was set between 25.86 baht to 25.90 baht Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, set its mid-rate for the dollar at 25.88 baht, up from 25.85 baht Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said both foreign and local investors actively sought the dollar, pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its high for the day at 25.940 baht - a level not seen since January 1992 - at 0430 GMT (12.30 a.m. EDT Tuesday). However, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped drag the dollar off its high and closed slightly above its Monday's level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Investors dumped the baht in favor of dollars amid uncertainty surrounding the leadership of the finance ministry and his indepedence in implementing necessary economic policy, said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. Such uncertainty arose from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh, who is assuming the supervisory role in the country's economic management. \par \par \uc2  'Investors were wondering what's really going on with the finance minister and whether he will be replaced,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1104GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 7:51 ET) \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5d03gsz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
