\par\par \b \uc2  Amnuay says  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  not propping up baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 9 (Reuter) - Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said on Friday the baht rallied against a weakening U.S. dollar in line with market forces and he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to artificially prop up the Thai unit. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay said the official baht/dollar midrate fixed by the Bank of Thailand at 25.99 on Friday, against 26.05 on Thursday, reflected the U.S. dollar's movement in major markets. \par \par \uc2  The minister told reporters: "I do not believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take actions to resist market mechanism." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Singapore said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  there on Friday morning by selling dollars at 26.025 baht after the Thai unit came under intense pressure on rumours it denied of a baht band widening. \par \par \uc2  Amnuay's remark followed an earlier repeated denial by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials of rumours of a change in Thailand's exchange rate mechanism. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement late on Friday that the Thai economy was moving in the right direction with an improvement in price stability. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 25.975/26.025 to the dollar late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662)-6520642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5905uut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
