\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand's SET index breaks through 600-pt level. \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 9 (Reuter) - Thailand's SET index broke through the key psychological level of 600 late on Friday morning as economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns saw continued sales of bank and finance stocks by foreign investors, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The SET Index dropped 14.07 points, or 2.29 percent, to 599.97 by 0429 GMT. The SET 50 fell 01.10 points, or 2.44 percent to 43.29. Turnover was 950 million baht. \par \par \uc2  Renewed market speculation on \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's baht fixing practice after reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore this morning and worries about economic fundamentals undermined sentiment, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  "Foreigners are still selling banks as they have been most of the week. We are checking on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumours but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a worry again," said a trader at a brokerage firm affiliated with Thai Farmers Bank. \par \par \uc2  Weak economic growth, export and corporate earnings outlooks, as well as liquidity and asset quality problems in the finance sector weighed on sentiment, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Texas Instruments Inc 's attribution of Thai economic problems as a factor for its withdrawal from joint ventures with Alphatec Electronics Plc was a further negative factor, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Alphatec was limit down 6.50 baht to 59.50, Asia Credit dropped 7.50 to a year low of 76.50, TISCO also hit limit low, falling 5.25 to 48.75. \par \par \uc2  Banks lost 2.84 percent by 0512 GMT. Bangkok Bank fell three to 160, Thai Farmers four to 107. \par \par \uc2  The index regained some ground to 602.44 by 0512 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -- James Mclean (662) 652-0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5905usj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
