\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Up In Early Trade As Dlr Drops VS Yen, DM \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1997\par 05:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is recovering against the U.S. dollar in early Asian spot trading Wednesday after six sessions of decline, benefiting from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against the Japanese yen and the Deutsche mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also stronger in the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums are dropping as the pace of dollar-buying slowed down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0240 GMT (10:40 p.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at 26.122 baht, down from 26.130 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, the dollar is still trading outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the dollar to move against the baht, indicating that the market remains bullish on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The band was set between 26.08 baht and 26.12 baht Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its daily mid-rate for the dollar at 26.10 baht, down from 26.11 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Because the baht is pegged to the dollar-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Thailand lowered its midrate for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and allowed the baht to strengthen, after the dollar weakened against the mark and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at 126.88 yen, down from 126.93 yen late in New York Tuesday. At the same time, the dollar is also at 1.7235 marks, down from 1.7263 marks Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates, meanwhile, are stable at 7%, from 6%-7% Tuesday, but are expected to drop amid growing money supply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0301GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4u033bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
