\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Baht Tumbles -3: Hurt By Dollar Strength Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 06:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Some dealers also expect the baht to drop further as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its ascent against the Japanese yen. The dollar rose to a 55-month high against the yen earlier this morning and continued to hover around that level at present. Around 0355 GMT (11:55 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at Y126.91, up from Y126.33 late in New York Tuesday. That was the highest dollar rate since Aug. 13, 1992. \par \par \uc2  Because of that, later dollar/baht trading may be influenced by the dollar's ascent against the yen as investors will likely begin to discount the impact from the credit rating downgrade, said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  'The initial reaction was negative, but I think investors will soon ignore the downgrade news and focus on the dollar's rise against the yen,' he said. 'This announcement has been expected for quite some time now.' \par \par \uc2  A spokeswoman for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't yet \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the baht and declined to comment whether the bank will later on. \par \par \uc2  'I think they (Moody's) must have reviewed the matter carefully before they made their decision,' said Duangmanee Wongprathip, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman. 'We haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and will have to decide later what to do.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0411GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902fqt\par 