\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Falls Early As Dlr Hits 55-Mo High VS Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 05:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is falling against the dollar in early spot trading Wednesday, a result of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge against the Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is stronger in the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums are mostly lower, resulting from increasing supply of money in the interbank market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0245 GMT (10:45 p.m. EDT, Tuesday), the dollar is at 26.103 baht, up from 26.093 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. At that level, the dollar is trading slightly above the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 26.06 baht and 26.10, indicating strong demand for dollars in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed its daily midrate for the dollar at 26.08 baht, up from 26.06 baht Tuesday. That was the highest midrate since Sept. 11, 1989. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors continued to sell baht in favor of dollars, betting on the persistent strength of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar has been rising against the yen in recent sessions, sending it to the highest level in 55 months of Y126.80 at 0201 GMT (10:01 p.m. EDT) Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'It looks like the dollar will continue to rise against the yen,' said a dealer at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in Bangkok. As a result, downward pressure on the baht is expected to remain in the near term, he added. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 80% of which is dominated by the U.S. dollar. Because of the peg, the Bank of Thailand increases its daily midrate for the dollar when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket, allowing the dollar to rise.< \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0301GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902ffy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
