\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Falls Early After Dlr Hits 50-Mo High Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par 04:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is falling against the dollar in early Asian spot trading Tuesday, hurt by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it hit a 50-month high against the Japanese yen earlier in the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is mixed in the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. One- and two-month swap premiums are rising, but the three-, six-month and one-year rates are lower, suggesting that the dollar isn't as popular in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at 26.058 baht in the spot market, up sharply from 25.977 baht at the close of trading Friday. Thai financial markets were closed on Monday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  At that level, the dollar is trading within the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 26.04 baht and 26.08, indicating that demand for dollars in the spot market remains moderate. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed its daily midrate for the dollar at 26.06 baht, up from 25.94 baht Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht weakened after the dollar reached a 50-month high against the yen earlier in the session. At 0230 GMT, the dollar is trading at Y125.65, below Y125.85 around 0001 GMT (8:31 p.m. EDT) Tuesday, but still higher than Y125.63 late in New York Monday. The dollar's rate at 0001 GMT was the highest level since Jan. 15, 1993. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 80% of which is dominated by the U.S. dollar. Because of the peg, the Bank of Thailand increases its daily midrate for the dollar when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket, allowing the dollar to rise against the baht as a result. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0245GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4802ec5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
