\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Lower After U.S. Treasury's Rubin Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 1997\par 04:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is sliding against the dollar in early Asian spot trading Friday as investors rushed to buy U.S. dollars in a wake of remarks by the U.S. Treasury Secretary reflecting U.S. concerns over the widening trade gap between the U.S. and Japan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a result, also weakened in the swap market where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums are rising amid increasing demand for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0220 GMT (9:20 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 25.959 baht in the spot market, up from 25.955 baht at the close of trading Thursday. At that level, the dollar is trading close to the ceiling of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.96 baht. That, dealers said, indicated rising demand for dollars in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its dollar-baht fixing rate at 25.94 baht Friday, unchanged from Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also remained unchanged at 25.92 baht and 25.96 baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar-buying picked up after U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin commented that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate shouldn't be used as a trade tool. His remarks, dealers said, was dollar-bullish, prompting investors to shift to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates, however, are dropping after banks completed their reserve reporting for the coming week. Banks are required to deposit 7% of their funds with the Bank of Thailand on the 7th and 22nd of every month. But because the 7th is a holiday in Thailand, many banks have attemted to meet the requirement early. \par \par \uc2  Both the overnight interbank and call rates dropped to 8.5%-9.0%, down from 9.5%-10.0% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0241GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4402g7l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
