\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Lower Early On Active Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1997\par 05:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is dropping against the dollar in early Asian spot trading Thursday as investors are buying dollars on short-covering, while others are abandoning the baht for fears that the downgrade of Thailand's long-term credit rating will be announced next week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is stronger in the swap market where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums continue to drop amid expectation of increasing money supply in the interbank market, following the launch of the 72 billion-baht government pension fund, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0240 GMT (9:40 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 25.961 baht in the spot market, up from 25.923 baht at the close of trading Wednesday. At that level, the dollar is trading slightly above the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.92 baht to 25.96 baht, indicating strong demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its dollar-baht fixing rate at 25.94 baht Thursday, up from 25.92 baht Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many investors who sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week are now accumulating dollars in the spot market on short-covering. Meanwhile, some investors are becoming cautious about the baht amid expectation that Moody's Investors Service, an international credit rating agency, will anounce the downgrade of Thailand's long-term credit-rating some time next week. \par \par \uc2  'Investors are being extremely careful about the short-term prospect of the baht,' said a dealer at a Japanese bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  In February, Moody's placed Thailand's sovereign foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceiling rating of A-2 on review for possible downgrade. As the government is scheduled to launch a roadshow for its $500 million to $700 million in Yankee bonds early next week, analysts are now expecting the downgrade to be announced at the same time. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0305GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4302hj6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
