\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand: Baht Higher In Early Trade On Tight Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 1997\par 05:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht is strengthening against the dollar in early Asian spot trading Wednesday as commercial banks sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid tightening money supply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also stronger in the swap market where investors agree to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums are dropping amid declining demand for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0240 GMT (9:40 p.m. EST), the dollar is at 25.929 baht, down from 25.955 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. At that level, the dollar is trading within the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.90 baht to 25.94 baht. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its dollar-baht fixing rate at 25.92 baht Wednesday, down from 25.96 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said tight money supply promoted commercial banks to sell dollars in favor of baht, seeking to improve their cash flow ahead of the long weekend. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's financial markets will be closed Monday for public holiday. Such a holiday coincides with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deadline for reserve reporting period, during which banks are required to deposit 7% of their funds with the Bank of Thailand. As a result, many banks also reduced lending in the interbank market, pushing interbank rates higher, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates are at 9.5%-10.0%, up from 9.5% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0240 GMT (9.40 p.m. EST), swap rates are as follows, in satang (1\par baht equals 100 satang):\par        Wednesday    Tuesday     Monday      Friday\par 1 mo.  7.0-8.0      8.0-8.75    7.5-7.75    6.0-7.0\par 2 mo.  14.5-15.5    15.25-16.0  15.25-16.0  13.0-14.0\par 3 mo.  23.0-24.0    23.5-24.5   23.0-24.0   22.0-23.0\par 6 mo.  48.0-49.0    48.75-50.25 48.25-49.0  48.0-49.0\par 1-yr.  94.0-97.0    95.0-98.0   94.0-97.0   94.0-97.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-04-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0309GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4202bnd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
