\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Ends Lower In Spot Market As Dlr Gains Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht slipped against the dollar in Asian spot trading Wednesday, hurt by the U.S. dollar's advance against the Japanese yen and the Deutsche mark during the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  But the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums fell as investors sold dollars amid rising confidence in the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 25.945 baht in the spot market, up from 25.943 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. At that level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was well within the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.91 baht to 25.95 baht Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-rate for the dollar was 25.93 baht. \par \par \uc2  The baht is pegged to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  consisting of the dollar, the yen and the mark. It tends to fall when the dollar rises against the other two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At the close of Asian trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 123.13 yen, up from 122.43 yen at the close of trading in New York Tuesday. The dollar was at 1.6817 marks, up from 1.6730 marks in New York Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates fell, meanwhile. The overnight and call rates were both at 8.5% to 9%, down from 9% to 9.25% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates were as follows, in satang (1 baht equals 100 