\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Ends Higher Late On Short-Covering Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht rose in late Asian trading Tuesday as investors returned to the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a panic over the downgrade of two Thai banks' credit ratings receded, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The baht, however, slipped in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell dollars at specified times in the future. Swap premiums rose as demand for dollars in the future rose on expectations that the U.S. interest rates would rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Tuesday, the dollar was at 25.943 baht, slightly below 25.945 baht on Monday. At that level, the dollar was trading within the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 25.95 to 25.99 baht Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, kept its midrate unchanged at 25.97 baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht weakened earlier in the morning session on a selloff, triggered by news that Standard & Poor's had cut credit ratings of two Thai banks and placed two more on creditwatch for a possible downgrade. However, many investors bought back the baht in the afternoon for short-covering after the panic receded, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'Investors sold the baht earlier on the downgrade news, but the reaction was brief,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. 'They came back after seeing that the country's short- and long-term debt ratings weren't affected.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1109GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3